  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Phenylmercuric borate and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, as it is indirectly linked through a series of molecular targets. Phenylmercuric borate is identified as a target of ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3, which in turn is a target of dihydroepoxyalantolactone and vitexifolin D. Both dihydroepoxyalantolactone and vitexifolin D are known to interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, indicating a possible pathway through which Phenylmercuric borate may influence this enzyme. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights the role of secondary metabolites in modulating enzyme activity, but further experimental validation is needed to establish a direct causal link between Phenylmercuric borate and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4.",
